\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Each layer's real, measured contribution to overall detection is a different size -- and CP's is exactly zero, visibly.} Defense-in-depth staircase, ITE-Bench ($n{=}9{,}900$, Table~\ref {tab:ite_ablation}): overall recall as layers are added in order, on the one benchmark spanning communication, behavioral, and semantic attacks together. B1 alone closes the communication class (recall $0.381$); adding B2 closes the behavioral class (+$0.286$); adding CP contributes exactly $+0.000$, the disclosed data-generation gap (Section~\ref {sec:limitations}), shown as a flat step rather than a symbol; the full stack (adding B3 and the Trust Decision Engine) closes the remaining semantic class (+$0.333$, recall $1.000$). Right: the same final checkpoint's Trust Decision Engine, live CARLA (Table~\ref {tab:carla}, this pass's freshly-rerun final-checkpoint results) -- every real attack scenario is flagged, two by B3 directly and two more by MBD's backstop where B3 remains invisible to raw event tags (Section~\ref {sec:limitations}). Every value is copied directly from Table~\ref {tab:ite_ablation} and Table~\ref {tab:carla}; no new metric was computed for this figure (\texttt  {LAYER\_FIGURE\_REDESIGN.md}).}}{5}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig_layer_responsibility}{{2}{5}{}{figure.2}{}}
